{title: 500 - Take Time to Be Holy}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #500 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 500}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F/C]Take [C7/Bb]time to be holy, [F/A]Speak oft with thy Lord;
[F/A]Abide [C7/Bb]in Him always, [C]And feed on His word;
[C7]Make friends of God's [Am]children, [Gm]Help [C]those [Am]who [C7]are [Bb]weak,
[Bb/D]Forgetting [C7]in [F/A]nothing His blessing to seek.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F/C]Take [C7/Bb]time to [F/C]be holy,
[F/C]the [C7/Bb]world rushes [F/A]on;
[F/A]spend [C7/Bb]much time [F/C]in [C]secret
[F/A]with [C7/Bb]Jesus [C]alone.
[C7]By looking [Gm]to [C]Jesus,
[C7]like him [Gm]thou [C]shalt [C7]be;
[Bb/D]thy [C7]friends [F/A]in thy conduct
[Bb/D]his [C7]likeness [F]shall see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F/C]Take [C7/Bb]time to [F/C]be holy,
[F/C]let [C7/Bb]him be [F/A]thy guide,
[F/A]and [C7/Bb]run not [F/C]before [C]him,
[F/A]whatever [C]betide.
[C7]In joy [Am]or [Gm]in [C]sorrow,
[C7]still follow [C]the [C7]Lord,
[Bb/D]and, [C7]looking [F/A]to Jesus,
[Bb/D]still [C7]trust [F/A]in his word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F/C]Take [C7/Bb]time to [F/C]be holy,
[F/C]be [C7/Bb]calm in [F/A]thy soul,
[F/A]each [C7/Bb]thought and [F/C]each [C]motive
[F/A]beneath [C7]his [C]control.
[C7]Thus led [Am]by [Gm]his [C]spirit
[C7]to fountains [C]of [C7]love,
[Bb/D]thou [C7]soon [F/A]shalt be fitted
[Bb/D]for [C7]service [F/A]above.
{end_of_verse}
